From e3bb42f360523bd07bb263aa850e6e2296f7e4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BGP Simulation Contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:11:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(simulation): add interactive web simulation (Next.js
 control room + real-time socket.io engine)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add simulation/ — a self-contained operator NOC for the AI-Enhanced BGP
control plane that runs the full defense pipeline live with every subsystem
toggleable and every parameter editable at runtime.

- engine/ (Bun + Socket.IO, port 3010): 10-AS topology with valley-free
  semantics, 10-feature behavioral extractor, RF/LogReg classifier,
  6-criteria trust engine, policy actor (LP 100/80/50/0 + no-export),
  shadow validation, autonomous rollback, S1-S6 scenarios, A0-A4 ablations
- webapp/ (Next.js 16, port 3000): control room with topology graph,
  live RIB, attack panel + custom attack builder, analytics (recharts),
  A/B auto-benchmark, ablation lab, chaos drills with config fuzz,
  per-prefix watchlist alerting, forensic report export, time-travel
  replay, AI copilot, run archive (Prisma + SQLite)
- no Docker/FRR dependency: the research pipeline is fully simulated,
  making the S1-S6 lifecycle and A0-A4 ablation matrix reproducible in
  ~2 minutes with two 'bun run dev' processes
- README: new 'Interactive Web Simulation' section + repo tree entry;
  simulation/README.md has setup, architecture and concept mapping

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
