+# 🖥️ AI-Enhanced BGP — Interactive Web Simulation
+
+[![Next.js 16](https://img.shields.io/badge/Next.js-16-black.svg)](https://nextjs.org/)
+[![Bun](https://img.shields.io/badge/runtime-Bun-f472b6.svg)](https://bun.com/)
+[![Socket.IO](https://img.shields.io/badge/realtime-Socket.IO-010101.svg)](https://socket.io/)
+[![Prisma](https://img.shields.io/badge/db-Prisma%20%2B%20SQLite-2d3748.svg)](https://www.prisma.io/)
+
+A real-time, fully-interactive operator **NOC ("Control Room") for the
+AI-Enhanced BGP autonomous control plane**. Every subsystem of the research
+pipeline — telemetry, feature extraction, ML classification, the hybrid trust
+engine, policy actioning, shadow validation, and rollback — can be
+**toggled on/off and tuned live** while the simulation runs, making it an
+interactive companion to the paper's A0–A4 ablation matrix and S1–S6 attack
+scenarios.
+
+| Control Room | Analytics |
+| --- | --- |
+| ![Control Room](docs/img/control-room.png) | ![Analytics](docs/img/analytics.png) |
+
+---
+
+## ✨ What you can do
+
+- **Live 10-AS topology** — animated force-graph of AS65001–AS65010 with
+  attack paths, quarantine badges and per-AS drilldown
+- **Run the six canonical attack scenarios** (S1 direct hijack · S2 sub-prefix
+  /25 · S3 flapping · S4 YouTube 2008 · S5 Google 2017 leak · S6 Cloudflare
+  2019 leak) **or build a custom attack** (prefix, origin AS, path length,
+  flap rate, leak shape)
+- **Every knob editable at runtime**: ML model choice (RF / LogReg), trust
+  weights (Σ must equal 1.0), policy tier thresholds, shadow streak & dwell,
+  rollback ticks, telemetry FPR/noise — with live config-diff vs. the A4
+  baseline
+- **A/B auto-benchmark** — run the same scenario across two defense variants
+  and compare MTTD / MTTM / mitigation-success / RIB-verification
+- **Ablation Lab** — one-click A0–A4 variant runs with a survival-style
+  results matrix
+- **Chaos drills** — randomized scenario batteries with optional **config
+  fuzz** (defense knobs randomized per round, snapshot-restored after)
+- **Prefix drilldown & forensics** — per-prefix evidence trail, printable
+  incident report (browser print → PDF)
+- **Per-prefix watchlist** — star any route; status/trust-tier transitions
+  raise toasts, sound and visual alerts
+- **Time-travel replay** — scrub through the event history of a run
+- **AI Copilot** — an LLM assistant that explains what the defense system is
+  doing and answers operator questions about current state
+- **Persistence** — run archive (SQLite via Prisma) with KPI history,
+  presets for defense configs, full event-log export
+
+## 🏗️ Architecture
+
+```
+┌────────────────────────────┐        Socket.IO (path /, 800ms ticks)
+│  engine/   (Bun, port 3010)│◄──────────────────────────────┐
+│  · topology + valley-free  │   sim:state / event:new        │
+│  · 10-feature extractor    │───────────────────────────────►│
+│  · ML classifier (RF/LR)   │   attack:inject · config:update│
+│  · trust engine (Σw = 1.0) │   sim:start/pause/reset …      │
+│  · policy actor + shadow   │                                │
+│  · rollback engine         │        ┌───────────────────────┴──┐
+└────────────────────────────┘        │  webapp/  (Next.js :3000) │
+     SQLite (runs, presets) ◄───────── │  · control room + RIB     │
+        via REST /api/sim-runs         │  · analytics (recharts)   │
+        /api/sim-presets               │  · benchmark · copilot    │
+                                      └───────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+## 🚀 Quickstart
+
+Prerequisites: [Bun](https://bun.com/) ≥ 1.1.
+
+```bash
+# 1. start the simulation engine
+cd simulation/engine
+bun install
+bun run dev                 # Socket.IO on :3010
+
+# 2. start the web app (second terminal)
+cd ../webapp
+bun install
+cp .env.example .env        # DATABASE_URL for the run archive
+bunx prisma db push         # create the SQLite schema
+bun run dev                 # http://localhost:3000
+```
+
+The webapp connects to the engine through same-origin `/?XTransformPort=3010`
+(reverse-proxy mode). For a direct two-process deployment set:
+
+```bash
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BGP_SIM_URL=http://localhost:3010
+```
+
+in `webapp/.env` (engine CORS is open on localhost) — see
+`webapp/src/lib/bgp-sim/client.ts`.
+
+## 🗺️ Research-concept → feature mapping
+
+| Research concept (repo root) | Web simulation |
+| --- | --- |
+| 10-AS topology / Gao-Rexford | Topology graph + valley-free feature & policy guard |
+| 10-feature behavioral extractor | Live per-announcement feature panel |
+| Calibrated ML (4 classes) | Classifier card: model, sensitivity, class mix |
+| Hybrid trust engine (6 criteria) | Trust radar + weights editor (Σ=1.0 enforced) |
+| Policy tiers LP 100/80/50/0 | Route-map preview + RIB local-pref column |
+| Shadow validation + anti-thrash | Streak / dwell controls + quarantine badges |
+| Multi-criteria rollback | Rollback ticks control + LP restoration events |
+| S1–S6 scenarios | Attack panel one-click injection |
+| A0–A4 ablation matrix | Ablation Lab + auto-benchmark A/B |
+| MTTD / MTTM / MSR / RIB check | KPI header + benchmark result cards |
+| 12-week plan artifacts | Docs tab (architecture explainer) |
+
+## ⌨️ Operator conveniences
+
+Keyboard shortcuts (`?` cheat-sheet), sound alert modes (siren / chime / mute),
+dark control-room theme, mobile-responsive down to 390px, toast + watchlist
+alert history, CSV/HTML/JSON export of runs, printable forensic reports.
+
+## 📄 License
+
+MIT — same as the parent repository.
